--[[
    Terminalpanel Premium
    ------------------------------------------------------------
    Place this as a second LocalScript inside StarterPlayerScripts,
    alongside the main TerminalPanel script.

    This is a fully separate script on purpose: it has its own
    Luau 200-local-variable budget, independent of the main
    TerminalPanel script. All the admin-exclusive tools that used
    to live inside TerminalPanel (admincheck, check2, godmode) have
    been moved here so the main script has headroom again.

    If the local player's UserId isn't in ADMIN_USER_IDS below, this
    entire script does nothing at all — no UI is created, nothing is
    visible, nothing is discoverable. That's stronger hiding than
    per-command checks can offer, since there's no shared panel for
    a non-admin to even probe with command names.
--]]

local Players = game:GetService("Players")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local UserInputService = game:GetService("UserInputService")
local VirtualInputManager = game:GetService("VirtualInputManager")
local SoundService = game:GetService("SoundService")

local player = Players.LocalPlayer

-- Fill in your own UserId(s) here. This only hides the panel from
-- everyone else — it's a LocalScript check, so it can't be made
-- tamper-proof against someone editing their own client. True
-- enforcement would need a server Script + RemoteEvent.
local ADMIN_USER_IDS = {
	3101624536,
	11535922291,
	11517308890,
}

if not table.find(ADMIN_USER_IDS, player.UserId) then
	return -- not an admin: nothing below this line ever runs for you
end

